# Issue #1087 (milestone 3, C6/C9 end-to-end): the random_loss_5pct scenario with `transport ice`: the call is set up through
# the full stack (offer/answer, trickled candidates, ICE, DTLS) and its media goes as SRTP over the bundled transport
# on the same links. Its expect lines are random_loss_5pct's; the setup.* and transport.* lines check the connection.
# sm_compare runs the direct twin; this copy is not compared (`compare off`).

name ice_random_loss_5pct
describe 5% random loss on a 2 Mbps link with 40 ms one-way delay -- through ICE, DTLS-SRTP and SDP (transport ice, #1087)
transport ice
compare off
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2000kbps delay=40ms jitter=3ms loss=5% queue=300ms
expect audio.concealed_pct < 3
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect video.residual_loss_pct < 0.5
expect video.render_fps >= 25
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 2500
expect setup.connected == 1
expect transport.send_failures == 0
